  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding 3–5 wt% SiC to ZrB2 powder will reduce the required sintering temperature.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC addition promotes transient liquid-phase sintering in ZrB2.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiC addition will refine the ZrB2 microstructure.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiC addition will reduce porosity in the resulting ceramic.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC addition will produce a protective silicon-rich interfacial layer.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The silicon-rich interfacial layer will reduce failure during long-term exposure to liquid plating baths.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC-modified ZrB2 can be densified by reactive hot pressing at approximately 2050–2100 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional pure ZrB2 requires sintering temperatures above 2300 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A transient liquid phase accelerates particle rearrangement and diffusion during hot pressing.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Residual silicon at grain boundaries or surfaces may oxidize during service.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation of residual silicon may form a protective silicon-rich layer, possibly SiO2.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed silicon-rich layer will mitigate corrosion by the liquid plating bath.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC-modified ZrB2 sintered at 2050–2100 °C will have higher density than conventionally prepared single-phase ZrB2.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC-modified ZrB2 will contain fewer intrinsic pores than conventionally prepared single-phase ZrB2.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC-modified ZrB2 will retain better structural integrity during long-term plating-bath exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC-modified ZrB2 will have a lower incidence of eventual component failure than conventionally prepared single-phase ZrB2.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pure single-phase ZrB2 has higher porosity and eventually fails because of microstructural weaknesses during prolonged plating-bath exposure.",
